- Story & Context: Long after the order vacated the mountain abbey, local villagers whispered that the unpruned apple orchard still resonated in four-part harmony whenever seasonal rain hammered against the conservatory glass. A group of wandering musicians returned with field recorders to document the myth, discovering that the root systems had permanently warped the rusted ground cables into an endless, self-oscillating choir feedback loop. In the resulting master tape, an airy pop chorus floats above the mud and tape hiss, repeating the haunting refrain: "Drink the rain and hold the chord."
